      "type": "layout.comment",
      "name": "Original temporal references and measurement scope",
      "description": "Images, signals, pixel references and project are original OpenCVDataflowGUI contributor work, MIT. No customer or third-party media. Eight stationary 64x48 frames use a zero-mean signal with sample variance 4 and gains 1 and 2 in left/right halves. Paired Y has 3x signal plus orthogonal noise; green has 2x signal plus that noise. Default gray self-pair has covariance equal to variance. Counts/validity are per pixel. Paired sources explicitly assert matching pixel indices and share an external ticket; this fixture does not prove physical registration or exposure synchronization. Exponential weights are .25*.75^age; sample normalization uses W-sum(w\u00b2)/W. Run all from reset for the stated references. Ticket-mismatch and memory-limit projects deliberately emit no statistics. Temporal variation can include scene movement/lighting drift and is not automatically pure camera noise.",
